---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Help and recovery">
  <article class="guide wrap">
    <div class="guide-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">GUIDE / HELP & RECOVERY</p><h1>Let’s get you reconnected.</h1><p
        class="lede"
      >
        Change your Wi-Fi or reset a forgotten device password while keeping your prayer settings.
      </p>
    </div><div class="guide-body">
      <h2>Changed your Wi-Fi or forgot your password?</h2><ol>
        <li>Unplug the Pyramid’s bottom power cable.</li><li>
          Connect your computer to the Atom’s USB-C with a data cable.
        </li><li>
          Open <a href="/install/">device setup</a> in desktop Chrome or Edge and choose <strong
            >Fix Wi-Fi or password</strong
          >.
        </li><li>
          Choose <strong>Change Wi-Fi</strong> or <strong>Reset device password</strong>. The old
          device password is not needed over USB.
        </li><li>When done, unplug the Atom and reconnect only bottom power.</li>
      </ol><p>
        Password recovery signs out existing sessions. It does not reinstall firmware, reset prayer
        settings, or erase playback history.
      </p><h2>No device appears</h2><p>
        Check that your cable transfers data and is connected to the Atom’s port. Close other
        browser tabs or serial tools using the device. If you cancelled the browser picker, select
        the connection button again when ready.
      </p><h2>The port is busy or the connection drops</h2><p>
        Close other software using the USB port, reconnect the data cable, and start again. Opening
        or reopening USB has caused temporary Wi-Fi loss on the reference device. Allow time for it
        to reconnect before checking its local page.
      </p><h2>The Wi-Fi password did not work</h2><p>
        Check the network name and password. Use a 2.4 GHz WPA2/WPA3 personal network, rather than a
        guest sign-in portal or enterprise network. A rejected connection retains the previous saved
        credentials.
      </p><h2>The result is uncertain</h2><p>
        If the connection ends before an acknowledgement, the device may already have saved the
        change. The installer will not automatically send it again. Reconnect and check status
        before another change. A connected status alone may describe the previous network; it does
        not prove an uncertain Wi-Fi change succeeded.
      </p><p>
        For a password change, check the reported password revision and try signing in with the
        password you just chose. If you still cannot sign in, start a deliberate password recovery
        after checking the device state.
      </p><h2>The device reports a storage fault</h2><p>
        Stop making changes and keep the current data. Record the error text without including
        passwords and request help through the <a
          href="https://github.com/OpenAthan-Project/openathan/issues">firmware issue tracker</a
        >. Do not reinstall as a shortcut to repairing credentials.
      </p><h2>The settings page will not open</h2><p>
        Use the device’s exact address, not a generic <code>openathan.local</code>. Try the IP
        fallback from USB setup. Keep your phone on the same LAN; guest-network isolation can
        prevent access. An IP address may change after reconnecting, so read it again over USB if
        needed.
      </p><h2>Installation was interrupted</h2><p>
        First-time installation is currently gated on an approved release. When available, an
        interrupted installation will require a deliberate recovery step. If the installer says the
        write was verified but setup could not reconnect, use USB recovery rather than reinstalling.
        Do not restore an old full-flash backup as routine recovery: it can restore old prayer
        history.
      </p><p>
        The browser installer does not yet support firmware upgrades on existing devices. Physical
        installation, interrupted-flash recovery and preservation tests must pass before public
        installation is enabled.
      </p><div class="actions">
        <a class="button" href="/install/">Open USB recovery <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
        ><a href="/guides/setup/">Read the setup guide</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
